Third-party material: the IARU's ITU-zone definitions
-----------------------------------------------------

The file(s) src/itu_zones_mcp/data/published/IARURegion1HFManagerHandbook8.2.1.pdf
is the IARU Region 1 HF Managers Handbook, version 8.2
(https://www.iaru-r1.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/IARURegion1HFManagerHandbook8.2.1.pdf), by
IARU Region 1. Its chapter 9.8, "Definition of ITU-Zones when used by radio amateurs" (pages dated
November 2000), defines the ITU zones for amateur use under IARU Region 1 recommendation
REC/99/LH/C4.2; it was drafted by G3HTA from the ITU's CIRAF zones and approved by all three IARU
regions. The handbook is shipped unmodified; data/SOURCE.json records its SHA-256 and a test checks
the file against it.

data/facts/itu_zones.json holds facts from chapter 9.8 (zone numbers and the prefixes and areas
each covers, in the chapter's own words), each citing its page and zone. They are the IARU's.

This project's GPL-3.0-or-later licence covers our own code and files. It does not cover the
owner's published file(s) or the facts from them, and we claim no rights in them.

Ours: everything else in data/, which is our arrangement of the owner's facts and is labelled as
ours: data/SOURCE.json, data/owner-list.schema.json, data/derived/ (built from the facts) and
data/load.sql (generated).

Test material: tests/crosscheck/cty.dat is AD1C's country file (https://www.country-files.com/),
MIT licence, with its notice in tests/crosscheck/AD1C-LICENSE.txt. It is used only as a cross-check
in the tests and is not part of the published package.
